-- resident employee: chargeable 120,000 - 21,400 = 98,600; tax 3,350 + 18,600 x 11.5% = 5,489
#ASSERT (`the income tax position for` `a resident employee`)'s `resident in Singapore`
#ASSERT (`the income tax position for` `a resident employee`)'s `income charged` EQUALS 120000
#ASSERT (`the income tax position for` `a resident employee`)'s `income exempt` EQUALS 15000
#ASSERT (`the income tax position for` `a resident employee`)'s `personal reliefs` EQUALS 21400
#ASSERT (`the income tax position for` `a resident employee`)'s `chargeable income` EQUALS 98600
#ASSERT (`the income tax position for` `a resident employee`)'s `tax payable` EQUALS 5489
#ASSERT (`the income tax position for` `a resident employee`)'s `last day to pay` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 6 10)
#ASSERT (`the income tax position for` `a resident employee`)'s `late payment penalty` EQUALS 0
-- nothing paid by 10 June: 5% of 5,489
#ASSERT (`the income tax position for` `a resident employee who pays late`)'s `late payment penalty` EQUALS 274.45
-- s 42A(3): the rebate of 10,000 absorbs the 5,489
#ASSERT (`the income tax position for` `a resident employee with a rebate`)'s `tax payable` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`the income tax position for` `a resident employee with a rebate`)'s `rebates and remissions` EQUALS 5489
-- company: statutory 300,000 - 50,000 = 250,000; taxed 2,500 + 95,000 + 50,000 = 147,500 x 17% = 25,075;
-- s 92L: 50% = 12,537.50 less the 2,000 grant = 10,537.50 (below 38,000)
#ASSERT (`the income tax position for` `a trading company`)'s `statutory income` EQUALS 250000
#ASSERT (`the income tax position for` `a trading company`)'s `chargeable income` EQUALS 250000
#ASSERT (`the income tax position for` `a trading company`)'s `tax before rebates` EQUALS 25075
#ASSERT (`the income tax position for` `a trading company`)'s `tax payable` EQUALS 14537.5
-- start-up: 25,000 + 50,000 + 50,000 = 125,000 x 17% = 21,250; remission 10,625 - 2,000 = 8,625
#ASSERT (`the income tax position for` `a start-up company`)'s `tax before rebates` EQUALS 21250
#ASSERT (`the income tax position for` `a start-up company`)'s `tax payable` EQUALS 12625
-- the trade loss of 50,000 set against the rent 80,000: 30,000; taxed 2,500 + 10,000 = 12,500 x 17% = 2,125;
-- remission (no grant): lower of 1,062.50 and 40,000
#ASSERT (`the income tax position for` `a company with a trade loss`)'s `assessable income` EQUALS 30000
#ASSERT (`the income tax position for` `a company with a trade loss`)'s `tax before rebates` EQUALS 2125
#ASSERT (`the income tax position for` `a company with a trade loss`)'s `tax payable` EQUALS 1062.5
-- non-resident employee: s 40B, 15% x 50,000 = 7,500, more than a resident's 1,250
#ASSERT NOT (`the income tax position for` `a non-resident employee`)'s `resident in Singapore`
#ASSERT (`the income tax position for` `a non-resident employee`)'s `tax payable` EQUALS 7500
-- non-resident with rent: employment share 60%: 60,000 x 15% = 9,000 (resident 5,650 x 60% = 3,390 is less);
-- the other 40,000 at 24% = 9,600
#ASSERT (`the income tax position for` `a non-resident with rent`)'s `tax payable` EQUALS 18600
-- s 2A: unremitted foreign income is not charged: 50,000; no reliefs given; tax 550 + 10,000 x 7% = 1,250
#ASSERT (`the income tax position for` `a resident with unremitted foreign income`)'s `income charged` EQUALS 50000
#ASSERT (`the income tax position for` `a resident with unremitted foreign income`)'s `tax payable` EQUALS 1250
#ASSERT REFUSED `the income tax position for` `a taxpayer in YA 2023`
